cartridge "BIRD AND CATERPILLAR/CZES KOSNIOWSKI/1983"

' BIRD AND CATERPILLAR - ColecoVision version of the Oric game by Chris
' (Czes) Kosniowski ("Games to Play on Your Oric-1", Shiva, 1983, game 4).
' Adapted by Amy & Claude, Amy Studio 2026. Built by build.py from this
' file, ../_common/amy/core.alexis, pages.txt, art.py and music/*.txt.
'
' THE GAME (as in the book): a caterpillar of three segments crawls without
' stopping; the joystick turns it. It eats the berry (ZAP, one more bit of
' food, a new berry somewhere else). A bird hops one cell at a time, most
' of the time (70 %) towards the berry - if it gets there first, the berry
' moves - and otherwise towards the caterpillar's head. The caterpillar
' dies when it hits the hedge ("got squashed"), bites itself (going
' straight back is a bite, as in the book) or meets the bird ("the bird
' ate the caterpillar"). The end shows how many bits of food it ate.
'
' CONTROLS: joystick only. Title: up/down choose, left/right change the
' starting level, a button confirms.
'
' LIBERTIES (listed for Amy):
' - Play field: columns 3-28, rows 3-21 inside a hedge (the book's 36 x 25
'   inside a frame of inverse blocks); HUD on row 1.
' - Levels: eight berries clear a level (the book went on forever). Three
'   caterpillars (lives) instead of one go; a death restarts the level
'   with the berries already eaten kept.
' - Level 1 is the book's game with a calmer bird: the caterpillar keeps
'   the book's three segments, crawls 6 cells a second, and the bird hops
'   one cell every 36 frames (in the book they moved in step). Later
'   levels: a longer caterpillar (+1 every two levels, up to 10), a faster
'   crawl, a quicker bird that comes for the head more often (tables for
'   levels 1-16, then the last value; checked with tests/bot.mjs).
' - The bird's hop is shown in flight (8 frames); it lands on its new cell
'   at the end of the hop, and that is when it eats or catches anything.
' - A new berry never appears within 6 cells of the bird.
' - Colour, animation, music and sound effects are new; the Oric's ZAP,
'   EXPLODE and the three paper flashes of a death are kept as the cues.

